      "identified_speaker": "Charlie",
      "similarity_score": 0.9546921789880186
    },
    {
      "start": 136.722,
      "end": 148.086,
      "text": "He tells us that at this festive season of the year, with Christmas and roast beef looming before us, similes drawn from eating and its results occur most readily to the mind.",
      "speaker_label": "SPEAKER_01",
      "identified_speaker": "Charlie",
      "similarity_score": 0.9790752362995244
    },
    {
      "start": 149.487,
      "end": 151.468,
      "text": "The old man's eyes remain fixed on the door.",
      "speaker_label": "SPEAKER_03",
      "identified_speaker": "Alice",
      "similarity_score": 0.8623751120292666
    },
    {
      "start": 165.856,
      "end": 174.662,
      "text": "He has graved oats, whether Sir Frederick Layton's work is really Greek after all, and can discover in it but little of Rocky Ithaca.",
